# bead bpp: port LibreLane 2.4.13's OpenROAD Tcl scripts to run on the OpenROAD 26Q2
# binary shimmed onto PATH by pnr/Makefile's check-asap7-openroad (bead ocm).
#
# Scope: the "corners -> scenes" API rename family (rsz::check_corner_wire_cap ->
# est::check_corner_wire_caps, sta::corners -> sta::scenes, sta::set_cmd_corner ->
# sta::set_cmd_scene, utl::metric_int -> utl::metric_integer); a related but separate
# defect found only by an actual PnR-stage run, not by the namespace sweep -- under
# 26Q2, [sta::scenes] returns plain NAME STRINGS, not command objects, so every
# `[$corner name]` method call (45x in corner.tcl, 2x in common/io.tcl) fails with
# "invalid command name <scene-name>"; and one related argument-level deprecation
# (detailed_route / pin_access -bottom_routing_layer / -top_routing_layer ->
# set_routing_layers), checked by reading 26Q2's proc bodies but not run end-to-end.
#
# Every guard keys off `[info commands <new-name>]` (or, for the corner-name and
# drt.tcl fixes, off `[info commands sta::scenes]` as a version-capability proxy,
# since those are argument/return-shape changes with no namespaced existence check of
# their own) so the SAME scripts run unmodified on BOTH the bundled OpenROAD
# (edf00dff) + OpenSTA 2.6.0 in LibreLane 2.4.13's own nix-shell, AND on the 26Q2
# binary shimmed in by check-asap7-openroad. No hard version-string switch anywhere.
#
# Base: this diff is relative to the LIVE ~/Downloads/Github/librelane tree's state AS
# OF 2026-09-15 (i.e. it stacks on top of the already-applied bead-ocm/xy6/4l8/58q
# local patches -- PSM parser, ioplacer -random_seed, pdn.tcl decomposed build_grids,
# set_rc.tcl ASAP7 RC-injection fallback for RSZ-0089, drt.tcl catch-wrapper, and the
# Synlig/UHDM hierarchy-check + lib-sort + SYNTH_SHARE_RESOURCES fixes in
# synthesize.py/steps/pyosys.py/steps/odb.py -- it does not re-supply any of those).
# Apply after those, or directly to the live tree in its current (dirty) state.
# NOTE: set_rc.tcl is NOT included in this diff (it is an unrelated, already-existing
# local patch, not part of this bead's changes) but IS a hard prerequisite for any
# ASAP7 run past Global Placement -- see bead bpp notes for how it was rediscovered
# mid-session after being left off an initial three-item carryover list.
#
# Validation (bead bpp, 2026-09-15), full detail in bead bpp notes and knowledge.md:
#   1. pnr/asap7/valu_rtl (--to OpenROAD.STAPrePNR) on 26Q2 via the copy: exact match
#      to the known-good bundled-toolchain baseline (54634 inst / 4655.15 um^2 /
#      14.147 mW / WS -54.3 ps). NOTE: STAPrePNR/STAPostPNR (MultiCornerSTA) run
#      sta/corner.tcl through the standalone `sta` binary, which the ASAP7 shim pins
#      to OpenSTA 2.6.0 (NOT 26Q2) regardless of ASAP7_OPENROAD_BIN -- so this run
#      validated corner.tcl's *old*-toolchain path only, not the scenes path. It does
#      not by itself prove the scenes-side fixes; item 3 below does.
#   2. The SAME copy, SAME config, run again with no shim on PATH at all (LibreLane's
#      own OpenROAD edf00dff + OpenSTA 2.6.0): metrics BYTE-IDENTICAL to (1). Confirms
#      the guards are a true no-op on the old toolchain.
#   3. ASAP7 CPU block (rv32i_cpu_top, 10 SRAM macro instances), detached
#      (systemd-run --user --scope, MemoryMax=6G): OpenROAD.STAMidPNR (a plain
#      OpenROADStep run through the `openroad` binary itself -- 26Q2, real `ord`
#      namespace, real `sta::scenes`) first FAILED with exactly the `[$corner name]`
#      defect above; fixed with the ol_compat_corner_name guard; re-run of just that
#      step (--only OpenROAD.STAMidPNR --last-run) then PASSED cleanly (exit 0). Full
#      flow resumed --from OpenROAD.STAMidPNR --to OpenROAD.CTS to complete the CTS
#      validation -- see bead bpp notes for the final outcome/metrics.
#   4. drt.tcl's set_routing_layers / detailed_route argument fix is NOT validated by
#      an actual full-routing run in this session (out of scope: none of the runs
#      above reach OpenROAD.DetailedRouting). Checked only via `info body
#      detailed_route` / `info body pin_access` on the 26Q2 binary, which show
#      -bottom_routing_layer/-top_routing_layer raising unconditional utl::error
#      DRT-509/DRT-510 ("... is deprecated. Use set_routing_layers command instead.").
#      Re-validate with a real DRT run before relying on it.
#
# Also checked per bead ocm's other two notes, no defect found / no fix needed:
#   - "make_tracks must precede place_pin": already true in 2.4.13's Classic flow --
#     OpenROAD.Floorplan (which sources TRACKS_INFO_FILE_PROCESSED, containing the
#     make_tracks calls) runs at flow position 53, OpenROAD.IOPlacement at position 64.
#   - A full sweep of every `<namespace>::<proc>` call under librelane/scripts/openroad/
#     (28 distinct names) against 26Q2's `info commands` found exactly the same four
#     missing commands already tracked in bead bpp -- no additional MISSING-COMMAND
#     breakage beyond those four (the corner-name and routing-layer-argument defects
#     above are argument/return-shape changes on commands that still exist under both
#     names, so a plain `info commands` sweep cannot find them by itself).

--- a/librelane/scripts/openroad/common/io.tcl	2026-03-14 10:53:58.508115009 +0700
+++ b/librelane/scripts/openroad/common/io.tcl	2026-09-15 21:42:46.373851229 +0700
