+# pin_access proc bodies via `info body`). OpenROAD 26Q2 made -bottom_routing_layer /
+# -top_routing_layer on both detailed_route and pin_access hard errors:
+#   [ERROR DRT-0509] -bottom_routing_layer is deprecated. Use set_routing_layers instead.
+#   [ERROR DRT-0510] -top_routing_layer is deprecated. Use set_routing_layers instead.
+# (confirmed via bead ocm). set_routing_layers is the same command common/set_routing_layers.tcl
+# already uses ahead of global routing, and each LibreLane OpenROAD step runs in its own fresh
+# `openroad -exit` process (drt.tcl calls read_current_odb above), so any set_routing_layers
+# call made by an earlier step's process does not carry over -- it must be (re)issued here.
+# Gate on [info commands sta::scenes] as the same "is this 26Q2-class OpenROAD" signal used
+# for the corners->scenes rename elsewhere in this patch, since both changes ship together in
+# the same OpenROAD vintage and detailed_route/pin_access do not offer their own namespaced
+# existence check for this argument-level deprecation.
+if { [llength [info commands sta::scenes]] } {
+    set_routing_layers -signal [subst $min_layer]-[subst $max_layer]
+    if {[catch {
+        detailed_route\
+            -output_drc $::env(STEP_DIR)/$::env(DESIGN_NAME).drc\
+            -droute_end_iter $::env(DRT_OPT_ITERS)\
+            -or_seed 42\
+            -verbose 1
+    } errmsg]} {
+        puts stderr "WARNING: detailed_route reported errors; continuing (DRT may be incomplete): $errmsg"
+    }
+} else {
